hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17717","Waki narrated to us, Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal al-Adawi, from Khalid ibn Umayr, a man among them, who said: I heard Utba ibn Ghazwan say: I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no food for us but the leaves of khibba, until the corners of our mouths were ulcerated."
"17718","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, Humayd, meaning Ibn Hilal, narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Umayr who said: Utba ibn Ghazwan addressed us. Bahz said: And before this time he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us. He said: He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, this world has announced its cutting off and has turned away swiftly, and nothing remains of it but dregs like the dregs of a vessel which its owner sips. And you are moving from it to an abode that has no passing away, so move with the best of what is present with you. It has been mentioned to us that a stone is thrown from the edge of Hell and falls in it for seventy years without reaching its bottom. By Allah, you will surely fill it. Do you find it strange. By Allah, it has been mentioned to us that what is between the two gateposts of Paradise is a journey of forty years, and a day will surely come upon it crowded with thronging. And I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no food for us but the leaves of trees, until the corners of our mouths were ulcerated. And I picked up a cloak and split it between me and Sad, so he wrapped himself with half of it and I wrapped myself with half of it. And none of us today but has become a governor of a city among the cities. And I seek refuge with Allah from being great in myself and small before Allah. And there was never a prophethood but it changed in succession until its end becomes kingship. And you will be tested, or you will come to know, the rulers after us."
